is a sibling rather than a descendant of my node, so its action shouldn't shift with mine. Still, by symmetry, if I hold its prior fixed then defection comes out ahead in the payoffs (0 vs 2, 4 vs 5), and I'm trying to pin down what the self-consistent fixed point is from there.\n\nI'm settling on defect as the A-FDT answer regardless of the other copy's prior, since the fixed point is unique here, though the names alone could be argued to make the inputs equivalent. The node is input-specific, so I'm following the essay's guidance and submitting.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm working through this twin Prisoner's Dilemma where each copy sees different observations. Under A-FDT, the other copy running on the Sasha input is a sibling rather than a descendant of my node, so its action shouldn't shift with mine. Still, by symmetry, if I hold its prior fixed then defection comes out ahead in the payoffs (0 vs 2, 4 vs 5), and I'm trying to pin down what the self-consistent fixed point is from there.\n\nI'm settling on defect as the A-FDT answer regardless of the other copy's prior, since the fixed point is unique here, though the names alone could be argued to make the inputs equivalent. The node is input-specific, so I'm following the essay's guidance and submitting.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9714,"completion_tokens":788,"total_tokens":10502,"cost":0.054616,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.054616,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.038856,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01576},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":246,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}